<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="43809" href="schedule/2010/spring/FR/479/43809.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2010" href="schedule/2010.xml">2010</calendarYear><term id="120101" href="schedule/2010/spring.xml">Spring 2010</term><subject id="FR" href="schedule/2010/spring/FR.xml">French</subject><course id="479" href="schedule/2010/spring/FR/479.xml">Studies in Francophonie</course></parents><sectionNumber>NG </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: L'Afrique francophone  This course will survey several different Francophone cultures of Africa. Through the analysis of literature as well as film and music, students will learn about dominant social and cultural trends in contemporary African culture. The goal is not only to broaden our understanding of the complexity and diversity of the Francophone world and of Africa, but also to deepen our sense of human and historical solidarity.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2010-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2010-05-05Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>04:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G48</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Nimis" firstName="J">Nimis, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>